[#:seon.task{:name "a-contract-refusal-prints-a-generated-example-of-the-whole-schema"
             :intent "A contract refusal on a wrong-type argument prints a generated :example of the whole schema (about 40 lines of fake data, e.g. `seon.cluster.boot/readiness` given a string). Done when the refusal shows the expected schema name and one dig form, with no generated example for large maps, asserted on the refusal's data. Seen again by lane loop-prove (86b7cdbbe, 2026-10-10): the examples are junk values that no caller could pass, such as [:./R tV] and N/j, so they mislead as well as bulk; a refusal that cannot show a valid example shows none."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/bounded-text seon.error/bounded-text}}
 #:seon.task{:name "printed-copies-stored-or-sent-instead-of-values"
             :intent "Values are printed (pr-str or `seon.render.value/bounded-text`) into strings that are then stored or sent as data: provider settings and usage stored as EDN text (turn record-attempt!), faults and errors clipped into system-turn and diagnostic text, batch sources, error message content, test member drift and accretion reports, a background call's source. Owner 2026-10-07: keep real values; the value printer is the only way we print, once, at the edge. Inventory class printed-copy, 35 sites (the REPL reply's four, findings, interrupted, out and note, now go through `seon.render.value/core-text` and `seon.print/string-literal`): turn.clj 6, error.clj 4, sci/eval.clj 4, batch.clj 2, cluster/boot.clj 2, test.clj 2, test/accretion.clj 2, src/my/background.clj 1, background.clj 1, cluster.clj 1, cluster/message.clj 1, cluster/prompt.clj 1, cluster/wake.clj 1, config.clj 1, env.clj 1, instrument.clj 1, mcp.clj 1, render.clj 1, render/value.clj 1, schema.clj 1. Done when each site stores or sends the value (or its reference) and the edge prints it through the value printer, and seon.repl-test asserts an evaluation printing 50 MB to stdout answers a reply under the printer's budget with a dig form to the output blob."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/bounded-text seon.error/bounded-text seon.repl/text seon.turn/record-attempt!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--print-sites.tsv" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "ad-hoc-text-clips-outside-the-printer"
             :intent "`seon.mcp/call` cuts a request to its first 200 characters as its source with subs, outside the value printer (the other site, `my.program/match-row`, is task `my.program/a-search-snippet-keeps-the-whole-line`). Owner 2026-10-07: no random clipping. Done when it keeps the whole request as data and the printer bounds what is shown, asserted by a seon.mcp-entrance-test call with a 10,000-character request whose recorded source holds all of it."
             :must-read #{seon.mcp/call seon.render.value/bounded-text seon.error/bounded-text}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--print-sites.tsv" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--notes.md"}}]
